  "findings": [
    "No new CopperStart, CPU, disk or engine correction established. The unchanged rebuilt ROM and Nitro-qualified runtime reach bounded mission gameplay.",
    "All three supplied ADFs are used through normal read-only DF0 replacements: disk 1 to 2, 2 to 3, then 3 back to 2. No guest-memory patch or state restoration.",
    "Early forward/fire inputs left the helicopter on the frigate. A read-only canonical CPU trace confirms that the guest received input 0x41. Reverse flight at 36002 clears the deck and permits departure. This is not treated as a replacement-ROM input failure.",
    "WinUAE 6.0.3 with native Kickstart 1.3 and the same ADF set reproduces the landed start, then departs with reverse flight. This separate interactive diagnostic is not a field-matched replay or physical hardware proof.",
    "Live F10 map entry/exit, mouse selection of status/mission panels, visible helicopter and shadow, scenery scrolling, turning, chain-gun consumption, Space weapon selection and Hydra consumption work under both ROMs.",
    "The final map shows fuel 89, power 600, guns 1161, Hydras 37 and Hellfires 8. Enemy destruction, rescue and objective completion are not established."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Supplied unlabeled three-ADF set only; archive labels do not establish pristine original-media or protection qualification.",
    "Bounded Air Superiority mission loading and initial flight/weapons/map interactions only. Combat kills, rescue, landing/refuelling, objective or campaign completion, later campaigns and password reload remain unqualified.",
    "No Hellfire launch, alternate co-pilot, mouse/keyboard flight control or every sound/movie setting qualified.",
    "Nonzero PCM is sample presence, not listening or audio-fidelity verification.",
    "Native Kickstart comparisons use the same engine; the separate WinUAE diagnostic is unmatched and neither is a physical hardware oracle.",
    "No host-throughput measurement, full hardware-timing claim or change to historical performance inputs, fingerprints or acceptance dispositions."
  ],
